24-02-16\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3498 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: SAP Fiori Launchpad - Pages and Spaces\nDescription: The SAP Fiori launchpad now offers merging of spaces or pages. Administrators can define spaces that should be merged in the Manage Launchpad Spaces app, or pages that should be merged in the Manage Launchpad Pages app.\",535\n82,\" 2024-02-18\nValid as Of: 2024-02-16\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3498 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: SAP Fiori Launchpad - Pages and Spaces\nDescription: The SAP Fiori launchpad now offers merging of spaces or pages. Administrators can define spaces that should be merged in the Manage Launchpad Spaces app, or pages that should be merged in the Manage Launchpad Pages app. Merging spaces or pages can be used for example to reduce the number of duplicate apps, pages or spaces for users. It can also be helpful if you want to enrich SAP-delivered spaces or pages with customer-defined content.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-02-18\nValid as Of: 2024-02-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2402\n\n--- Record 3499 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: SAP Fiori Launchpad - Pages and Spaces\nDescription: The SAP Fiori launchpad now offers merging of spaces or pages. Administrators can define spaces that should be merged in the Manage Launchpad Spaces app, or pages that should be merged in the Manage Launchpad Pages app. Merging spaces or pages can be used for example to reduce the number of duplicate apps, pages or spaces for users. It can also be helpful if you want to enrich SAP-delivered spaces or pages with customer-defined content.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-02-18\nValid as Of: 2024-02-16\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3500 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: UI Development\nDescription: For UI development with Visual Studio Code Extensions, the update to the new extension version is required. Please refer to note 3425883  for more information.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-02-18\nValid as Of: 2024-02-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2402\n\n\",487\n686,\"--- Record 2431 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse: Specifying \"\"Empty Key\"\" Key Definition for Table Types\nDescription: You can now specify Empty Key as a Primary Key Definition for a table type.  See Working with Table Types.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-08-16\nValid as Of: 2024-08-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2408\n\n--- Record 2432 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse: Working with the Core Schema Notation Model Object Type\nDescription: The Core Schema Notation Model workbench object is a container for the imported Core Schema Notation (CSN) documents and the derived CSN model. The CSN documents can be manually uploaded into the Core Schema Notation Model workbench object.  See Working with the Core Schema Notation Model.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-08-16\nValid as Of: 2024-08-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2408\n\n--- Record 2433 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Add Custom Logo to Fiori Launchpad\nDescription: You can now exchange the SAP logo in the SAP Fiori launchpad with a customer logo. For administrators, there is a new parameter COMPANY_LOGO_URL in the Manage Launchpad Settings app. Here, you can upload a logo from a file. This logo will replace the SAP logo for all users.  For more information, see Manage Launchpad Settings.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-08-16\nValid as Of: 2024-08-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2408\n\n--- Record 2434 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Annotation: ObjectModel.supportedCapabilities\nDescription: You can use this annotation to check whether or not the UI use case is supported. If supported, then either the creation of UI projections or alternatively the direct consumption in an UI service binding is possible. Otherwise, warnings or errors occur indicating that the UI usage is not supported and might lead to unexpected errors.  For more information, see the annotation documentation of the ObjectModel domain in KTD.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-08-16\nValid as Of: 2024-08-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2408\n\n--- Record 2435 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Annotation: Semantics.valueRange\nDescription: You can use this annotation to inform consumers about the value range of a CDS element, allowing to specify minimal and/or maximal values and indicate whether these are exclusive or inclusive. The annotation can be applied to all fully ordered data types, i.e. Characters, Strings, Numbers, or Data Types.  For more information, see the annotation documentation of the Semantics domain in KTD.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-08-16\nValid as Of: 2024-08-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2408\n\n--- Record 2436 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Annotation: UI.dataPoint.title\nDescription: You can use this annotation to define the title of a data point.  For more information, see the annotation documentation of the UI domain in KTD.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-08-16\nValid as Of: 2024-08-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2408\n\n--- Record 2437 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Business Configuration App without Transport Option\nDescription:     You can now select the transport option No Transport.      There is a new option to enable a transport request selection bar in the header toolbar.    See Generating a Business Configuration Maintenance Object with the Generate ABAP Repository Objects Wizard\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-08-16\nValid as Of: 2024-08-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2408\n\n--- Record 2438 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: CDS Reusable Measures & Filters\nDescription: Managing and aligning analytical reporting might be quite challenging for complex businesses. With the introduction of reusable measures and filters, you can define key figures, measures, formulas, filters and many more features centrally, based on your needs. Those reusable measures and filters can then be utilized by CDS view entities by referencing those reusable artifacts. This ensures a homogenous definition of complex calculations and consolidates existing coherences of your running business.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-08-16\nValid as Of: 2024-08-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2408\n\n--- Record 2439 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Communication Arrangements\nDescription: Communication arrangements now also support Communication Targets and Logical External Schema.  For more information, see   .\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType\",440\n516,\"--- Record 3021 ---\nComponent: Peppol Exchange\nEnvironment: Neo\nTitle: Enhancement to the service for Germany\nDescription: In the test environment, the schematron file for XRechnung has been updated to version 2.0.2. This version is compatible with XRechnung 3.0.1.  This update will be active in the production environment as of May 5, 2024.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-01\nValid as Of: 2024-04-29\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3022 ---\nComponent: Intelligent Situation Automation\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Changes to commerical model\nDescription: Intelligent Situation Automation is not part of the newly introduced SAP BTP Enterprise Agreement (BTPEA) commercial model. As such, this service is no longer available in the SAP Discovery Service Catalog.  If you are licensed with the Cloud Platform Enterprise Agreement (CPEA) commercial model, you can continue to use Intelligent Situation Automation without any interruption. New customers can subscribe to the service from SAP Store.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-04-25\nValid as Of: 2024-04-26\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3023 ---\nComponent: Mobile Services\nEnvironment: Neo\nTitle: nan\nDescription: (Version 2305 and 2405) Mobile Services recommendations have been added to SAP BTP, Neo Environment Security Recommendations (filter on the Mobile Services component).  See:    Application Authentication      SAP BTP, Neo Environment Security Recommendations    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-01\nValid as Of: 2024-04-26\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3024 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Apps\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Mobile\nDescription:   Fixed currentUser system variable to work on mobile.  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-04-26\nValid as Of: 2024-04-26\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3025 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Changing totalResults attribute calculation mechanism\nDescription: Identity Provisioning changed the mechanism for calculating the total count of users or groups returned by proxy systems when executing a SCIM Proxy endpoint request to read entities from a backend system.  As of now, if the backend system provides the actual value of the totalResults attribute and there is no condition defined in the read mapping transformation of the proxy system, this value will be returned in the response from the Identity Provisioning implementation of the Proxy System SCIM API.  Previously, the value of totalResults attribute was the sum of the request parameters startIndex and count. This calculation mechanism remains unchanged for backend systems which do not provide value for the totalResults attribute.  See: SAP Business Accelerator Hub: SAP Cloud Identity Services  Identity Provisioning Service  API Reference   Users/Groups\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-04-25\nValid as Of: 2024-04-25\nVersion: 26003\n\n--- Record 3026 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Custom Schemas\nDescription: You can assign and edit via the administration console the attributes from custom schemas. See Extensions and List and Edit User Details.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-04-25\nValid as Of: 2024-04-25\nVersion: 26003\n\n--- Record 3027 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Data type introduced for expressions in Identity Provisioning graphical editor\nDescription: The data type of all transformation expressions is now displayed in the Identity Provisioning graphical editor under the Mapping Configurations screen of Add Mapping and Edit Mapping dialogs.  Some expressions have predefined read-only values, like optional is always set to Boolean. Others, like constant, are configurable and can be set as String, Integer, Boolean, Object, StringArray, IntegerArray, BooleanArray and ObjectArray.  See Working with Graphical Editor.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-04-25\nValid as Of: 2024-04-25\nVersion: 26003\n\n--- Record 3028 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Feedback Survey\nDescription: The feedback survey that is available via the administration console is extended and now together with your experiences with Cloud Identity Services you can also let us know what you think about its documentation. The documentation feedback link is also available through the SAP Cloud Identity Services Product Page.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-04-25\nValid as Of: 2024-04-25\nVersion: 26003\n\n--- Record 3029 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Notifications\nDescription: You can sort the notifications that are visible at the top-right corner of the administration console by type, priority, and date.\nAction: Info\",426\n367,\"Type: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-09-03\nValid as Of: 2025-08-15\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2508\n\n--- Record 287 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Referenced SAPUI5 Version\nDescription: As part of hotfix collection 4 (which is used for the standard upgrade), SAPUI5 version 1.136.4 is used for the administrator’s SAP Fiori launchpad, SAP-delivered Fiori apps, and the custom-built SAP Fiori apps, which are deployed to the ABAP system.  See SAP BTP ABAP Environment – Maintenance Windows and Major Upgrade Windows in 2025 and SAP UI5\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-15\nValid as Of: 2025-08-15\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2508\n\n--- Record 288 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: SAP Fiori Launchpad: Manage Launchpad Spaces and Pages: Redesign and Renaming\nDescription: In the SAP Fiori launchpad, both the Manage Launchpad Spaces and Manage Launchpad Pages apps were redesigned. We adapted the overview pages to enhance working with spaces and space templates, as well as with pages and page templates. \"\"Predefined\"\" and \"\"SAP-Delivered\"\" were renamed to \"\"Templates\"\" to ensure consistent terminology between these apps, the Maintain Business Roles app and the ABAP Development Tools for space and page templates.  See Manage Launchpad Spaces and Manage Launchpad Pages.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-06-25\nValid as Of: 2025-08-15\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2508\n\n--- Record 289 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: SAP Fiori Launchpad: New Layout for Launchpad Shell Bar and Menus\nDescription: The layout of the SAP Fiori launchpad shell bar, user menu, notifications list, navigation menu and user settings was changed according to the current SAP Design System. The user experience was harmonized across different SAP products. The navigation menu was enhanced and is now part of the shell bar. It now offers access to My Home, Favorite Apps, My Spaces and All Spaces.   The sorting options in the notifications list were simplified. In addition, there is a new button to directly open the settings from here. The order of entries in the user menu as well as in the user settings has been adapted.  See User Menu, Shell and Shell Bar and Working with Notifications.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-07-07\nValid as Of: 2025-08-15\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2508\n\n--- Record 290 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Server-Sent Events in ABAP HTTP\nDescription: The ABAP HTTP client and server now support server-sent events (SSE). Which allows a server to send parts of the body of the response to the client without the client having to actively request them. After being sent by the server, the client can fetch them as they become available.  For more information, see Enabling Server-Sent Events.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-15\nValid as Of: 2025-08-15\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2508\n\n\",403\n803,\"  For more information, see Merging Pages and Merging Spaces.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-05-17\nValid as Of: 2024-05-17\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2405\n\n--- Record 2920 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: SAP Fiori Launchpad: User Names in Manage Views Dialog\nDescription: In the Manage Views dialog, the Created By column now displays the user name rather than the user ID.  See Manage Views.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-05-17\nValid as Of: 2024-05-17\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2405\n\n\",360\n\n\nOutput:\n", "role": "user"}], "parameters": {"model": "gpt-4o", "frequency_penalty": 0.0, "max_tokens": null, "n": 1, "presence_penalty": 0.0, "temperature": 0.0, "top_p": 1.0, "response_format": {"type": "json_object"}}}, "key": "chat_create_community_report_ed2c8202eae46da799cbe462f3c9246e65e9377ecf79b575171100fd9ada9ae3_v2"}